{
  "$comment": "Cut-out puppet rigs for story characters (Phase 1 pilot, 2026-10-22). Units are each SVG's own viewBox (measured on a grid render). `pnpm --filter @banyan/video rig-cast` writes src/art/cast/<id>.<part>.svg, all in the source's viewBox so parts stack exactly. A part is either `clip` (every path of the art, minus `skip`, clipped to a polygon: good for head and torso) or `shapes` (only those path indexes, drawn whole over a dark outline stroke that replaces the art's shared silhouette: good for limbs, which must move away from what overlaps them). `joint` rounds a limb cut into a capsule so bends hide the seam. `pivot` is where the part turns. `fill` lays a skin-coloured capsule under a limb's shapes, to cover notches where the source art let something (a braid) cross it. `plaits` are braid segments drawn in code where the source braid crossed the T-posed arm (the art there is cut out, or a squared dark bar would remain once the arm moves).",
